@startuml SQ-08
title SQ-08 Disconnect, reconnect & server failure [P mechanism — rules TBD OQ-GP-05]
participant "Competitor Client" as C
participant "Match Server" as MS
participant "Backend API" as B
== Disconnect ==
C ->x MS : connection lost (ENet timeout / app backgrounded)
MS -> MS : slot DISCONNECTED; top keeps simulating with zero input;\ngrace timer 15 s [P]
MS -> B : POST /internal/v1/matches/{id}/state {participantDisconnected}
== Reconnect within grace ==
C -> B : GET /v1/me/active-match
B --> C : {matchId, status: IN_PROGRESS}
C -> B : POST /v1/matches/{matchId}/tickets {role: COMPETITOR}
B -> B : verify participant; INSERT command TicketGrant
B --> C : {host, udpPort, ticket}
MS -> B : heartbeat
B --> MS : {commands: [TicketGrant]}
C -> MS : connect + C2S_Hello {ticket}
MS -> MS : rebind userId; cancel grace
MS --> C : S2C_Welcome + full snapshot (prediction re-seeded)
== Grace expired ==
MS -> MS : apply rule [TBD]: keep simulating (default proposal)\nor eliminate with reason DISCONNECT
== Match Server failure ==
B -> B : scheduler: instance heartbeat older than 10 s [P]
B -> B : game_match ABORTED (BR-013), instance OFFLINE
B -> C : Reverb: match.aborted
note over B : Backend restart is not a match failure:\nservers keep heartbeating once it is back;\nlate results for contact-lost matches are accepted (P).
@enduml
